.TH GB-PROXY 1 "August 2026" "GB-proxy 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gb-proxy \- adapt modern web content for GEOBENCH and SymZilla
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gb-proxy
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gb-proxy
is an extensible HTTP proxy with first-class integrations for both GEOBENCH and
SymZilla on SymbOS.  It also retains inherited support for other constrained
legacy web clients.  It simplifies HTML, rewrites links, and converts images
into formats supported by early computers.
.PP
The packaged systemd service listens only on the loopback interface by default.
Edit
.I /etc/sysconfig/gb-proxy
before exposing it to a trusted LAN.  The proxy is not intended to be exposed
directly to the public Internet.
.SH CLIENT SUPPORT
GEOBENCH uses the
.B geobench
preset to receive simplified HTML and GBPC images in
.BR BROWSER.APP .
.PP
SymZilla on SymbOS selects bounded DOX documents and SGX images per request; it
does not require a separate preset.  It requires SymbOS 3 or newer, a
network-enabled SymZilla build, and a compatible running Network Daemon.  A
single proxy process can therefore serve both client families without a
separate SymZilla service.
.PP
The clients contact GB-proxy over plain HTTP.  GB-proxy performs HTTP or HTTPS
requests to upstream sites and returns client-specific converted content.  Its
root URL is not a browsing interface; configure it as the client's proxy
endpoint.
.SH REMOTE MARKDOWN
GB-proxy renders remote Markdown for both client families.  GEOBENCH receives
simplified HTML, while SymZilla receives a bounded DOX representation.  A
response is recognized as Markdown when its media type is
.BR text/markdown ,
or one of the legacy
.BR text/x-markdown ,
.BR application/markdown ,
or
.B application/x-markdown
aliases.
For compatibility with simple file servers, a URL ending in
.B .md
or
.B .markdown
is also recognized when the server labels the response
.BR text/plain .
.PP
The safe subset includes headings, paragraphs, ordered and unordered lists,
emphasis, code spans and blocks, tables, links, and remote images.  Relative
link and image destinations are resolved against the final remote document URL
after redirects.  HTTP and HTTPS images use the same bounded conversion path
as images in HTML pages.
.PP
GEOBENCH retains simple table markup.  SymZilla renders the cell content in
reading order rather than as a grid.
.PP
Raw HTML embedded in Markdown is inactive and cannot create scripts, forms,
frames, links, image fetches, or other active elements.  Markdown forms are not
supported.  Excessively complex inline-code delimiter layouts are rejected
before parsing so a hostile document cannot monopolize a proxy worker.
.PP
Markdown support applies only to documents fetched through GB-proxy.  SymZilla
does not parse local
.B .MD
or
.B .MARKDOWN
files.  Convert local documents to DOX separately or serve them over HTTP with
one of the recognized content types.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--config " PATH
Load the Python configuration file at
.IR PATH .
.TP
.BI "--host " ADDRESS
Listen on
.IR ADDRESS .
The default is 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.BI "--port " PORT
Listen on
.IR PORT .
The default is 5001.
.TP
.BI "--advertise-host " HOST
Use
.I HOST
or an absolute HTTP URL when generating proxy links returned to clients.
.TP
.BI "--cache-dir " PATH
Store disposable converted resources under
.IR PATH .
.TP
.BI "--state-dir " PATH
Store persistent runtime state under
.IR PATH .
.TP
.BI "--threads " COUNT
Run the Waitress server with
.I COUNT
worker threads.  The default is one.  GB-proxy uses one process, and several
bundled extensions hold process-global conversation or override state; keep one
thread when using those extensions.
.TP
.B --check-config
Validate the selected configuration and exit without starting the server.
.TP
.B --version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show command-line help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GB_PROXY_CONFIG
Configuration path used when
.B --config
is not supplied.
.TP
.B GB_PROXY_HOST
Default listening address.
.TP
.B GB_PROXY_PORT
Default listening port.
.TP
.B GB_PROXY_CACHE_DIR
Default cache directory.
.TP
.B GB_PROXY_STATE_DIR
Default state directory.
.TP
.B GB_PROXY_ADVERTISE_HOST
Default host or HTTP URL used in generated proxy links.
.TP
.B GB_PROXY_THREADS
Default number of Waitress threads.
.TP
.B GB_PROXY_LOG_LEVEL
Python logging level.  The default is INFO.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/gb-proxy/config.py
System configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/sysconfig/gb-proxy
Service command-line settings.
.TP
.I /var/cache/gb-proxy
Packaged service cache directory.
.TP
.I /var/lib/gb-proxy
Packaged service state directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.service (5)
